      "explanation": "<p>The reaction of HNO<sub>3</sub> and P<sub>4</sub>O<sub>10</sub> produces N<sub>2</sub>O<sub>5</sub>.</p>\n<p>4HNO<sub>3</sub> + P<sub>4</sub>O<sub>10</sub> <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.262ex\" height=\"1.181ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -511 1000 522\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2192\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2192\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> 2N<sub>2</sub>O<sub>5</sub> + 4HPO<sub>3</sub></p>\n<p>The reaction of HNO<sub>3</sub> with P<sub>4</sub> does not yield N<sub>2</sub>O<sub>5</sub>.</p>\n<p>P<sub>4</sub> + 20 HNO<sub>3</sub> <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.262ex\" height=\"1.181ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -511 1000 522\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2192\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2192\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> 4H<sub>3</sub>PO<sub>4</sub> + 20 NO<sub>2</sub> + 4 H<sub>2</sub>O</p>\n<p>The structure of N<sub>2</sub>O<sub>5</sub> has one N<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>O<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>N bond, but no N<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>N bond. It is diamagnetic in nature.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l0imm6d7/cf88369b-b196-416d-9a19-621812804795/2b3538b0-9f24-11ec-b824-11481766c67e/file-1l0imm6d8.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l0imm6d7/cf88369b-b196-416d-9a19-621812804795/2b3538b0-9f24-11ec-b824-11481766c67e/file-1l0imm6d8.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2016 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - p-Block Elements Question 52 English Explanation\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l0imm6d7/cf88369b-b196-416d-9a19-621812804795/2b3538b0-9f24-11ec-b824-11481766c67e/file-1l0imm6d8.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l0imm6d7/cf88369b-b196-416d-9a19-621812804795